# Vires — The Conserved Vital Force (GPU Substrate Allocator)

> *Latin*: **vires** (plural of *vis*) — "available strength; resources;
> the forces one can bring to bear". Not a faculty of mind — the finite
> metabolic substrate that every faculty must draw from to act.

## Philosophical Role

The brain runs on ~20 W. That budget is fixed; what changes is *where*
the blood, oxygen, and glucose flow. Active regions pull substrate
toward themselves through neurovascular coupling — astrocyte-mediated,
demand-driven, and entirely below the level of consciousness. No
"decision" allocates the energy; the act of being active *is* the
request.

Vires is that **arterial** substrate layer for DeusRidet: it routes
**compute** — the metabolic delivery of GPU work. The scarce resource it
governs is GPU *throughput* (SM occupancy, kernel-launch ordering,
compute bandwidth). Every consumer — Sensus (auditus/visus), Cogitatio,
Vox, Somnium, and Conscientia itself — issues GPU work, and Vires
arbitrates the limited compute among the concurrent requests so that
foreground perception and prefill are never starved by background
refinement.

Vires is **not** a mental faculty and **not** a scheduler-of-intent. It
neither decides what to think nor selects what to attend to. It only
answers a metabolic question: *given these concurrent demands on a
finite GPU, who computes now?*

## Scope Boundary — Compute, Not Memory

Vires governs **GPU compute allocation only**. It does **not** manage GPU
memory as a whole. The unified 64 GB DRAM — model weights, KV cache,
long-term memory indices, every LLM-related allocation — is the domain of
**Memoria** (the hippocampus / memory system). Vires never sizes, evicts,
or relocates an LLM allocation.

The one memory-adjacent task Vires may own is **reclaiming the
metabolic waste of non-LLM GPU work**: the transient scratch / arenas
left by auditus, orator (DiariZen), vox, and somnium passes once they
complete. Even here Vires only touches substrate it handed out for
non-LLM compute; anything LLM-related is deferred to Memoria. This is the
glymphatic clearance of *non-LLM* by-products, never a general memory
manager.

## Two Sibling Drivers, Not a Hierarchy

Perception feeds two distinct autonomic quantities, side by side:

- **Vigilia** (lives in `src/conscientia/scheduler.*`) reads sensor
  *presence* (sound, camera, direct injection) and sets wakefulness —
  *how deeply awake should we be?*
- **Vires** (this subsystem) reads the *actual GPU requests* emitted by
  conscious content (auditus/visus/cogitatio/conscientia) and answers —
  *given these concurrent demands, who gets substrate now?*

They share a source (perception) but measure different things. They are
**siblings, not parent and child.** Vires does **not** read Vigilia, and
Vigilia does **not** read Vires.

## Why "Idle Feeds Dreaming" Is Emergent, Not Coupled

When wakefulness is low, foreground consumers simply stop issuing
requests. Vires then finds spare substrate and background refinement /
Somnium consolidation naturally fills it. This behaviour falls out of
the demand structure itself — Vires never queries wakefulness to make it
happen. "Even idle is thought" is realised without any cross-layer wire.

## Invariants

- **One-way isolation.** Vires never includes a Conscientia / Vigilia
  header and never reaches up into a consumer. Consumers submit work to
  Vires; Vires only routes compute.
- **Compute, not memory.** Vires allocates GPU throughput, never LLM
  memory. GPU memory as a whole belongs to Memoria. Vires' only memory
  task is reclaiming non-LLM GPU scratch it itself handed out.
- **Demand-driven.** Vires has no internal model of intent or wakefulness.
  Its only inputs are the live requests submitted by consumers and a
  static per-consumer priority class.
- **Foreground is never starved.** Background-class work yields within a
  bounded window so high-priority perception + prefill + decode always
  make progress.
- **Wakefulness throttling stays at the source.** Cutting GPU work when
  drowsy (e.g. `scheduler.h` `probe_threshold`) lives in the consumer
  (Conscientia), not in Vires. Vires only ever sees "fewer requests".
